WEBVTT

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.080
Good morning, everyone!

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.910
Wh-What's wrong, guys?

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.660
President! I'm afraid our company...

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.950
Our company... is out of money!

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.080
Oh, my, I think he froze up.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.910
That's not something a brand-new
president wants to hear.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.580
I can use a heal spell
if you're not well, President.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.540
S-Sorry. That was so sudden, it threw me off.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.540
When you say we're out of money,
you mean like, all of it?

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.540
We took the opportunity of your induction
to recalculate our earnings, but...

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.120
...we're deeper in the red than ever before.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.950
Th-This is...

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:58.830
We're rated "D-" by the Adventure Academy,
and were declared a cottage company!

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.700
We barely got "small business" before.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:06.290
Considering our management shuffle,
they might think we're unstable.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:12.040
I think we can still stay afloat!
Though, it might really hurt our wages...

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.830
The thing is, Guide has already reduced
our expenses to the bare minimum.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:18.950
Thank you!

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.620
Don't mention it!

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.750
But as a result, we can't repair
or purchase the equipment we need.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.580
If it degrades too much, we won't
be acknowledged as adventurers.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.750
We'd fail next inspection.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.500
If it's bad enough,
they'll revoke our licenses too.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.290
B-But there's equipment right there!

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:40.910
See? Like this sword.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.370
Oh! Be careful!

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:42.870
Huh?

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:47.830
If you get cut by that sword,
you'll be financially cursed for life!

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:53.620
It'll make your debts increase
by a 32.5% annual interest rate.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.370
Th-That's worse than a loan shark...

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.790
Talk about a dangerous decoration.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:04.120
And if stabbed by that spear,
it will ruin your love life forever.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:04.910
Wha--?!

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:09.200
Doesn't getting hit by that hammer
make you weak and sickly?

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.250
Yeah. And being stabbed by that dagger
makes you laugh at everything you see.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:18.790
Wh-Why is all this stuff out in the open?

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:21.950
Collecting arms and armor
was the old man's hobby.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.450
It's too bad he didn't leave
behind anything useful.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.450
There're actually a lot of useful things he kept.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.330
Huh? Really?

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.910
That's news to me.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:36.080
What do you mean, Guide?

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:41.040
He kept all sorts of equipment
he brought back from dungeons, but...

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:41.950
But?

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.870
A little while before the rest of
you guys joined the company,

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.200
he donated all of it to a museum!

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.790
Wh-Why to a museum?

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.370
Do you think we can get it back?

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.450
If we go through the right channels,
I believe so.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:02.160
Then, let's go! If he had stuff, let's use it!

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.290
I don't want Yutoria to be sad again!

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.200
President...

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.120
--Yeah! I win!
--Like when you were young
and got crushed at board games,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.250
--Like when you were young
and got crushed at board games,

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.330
bawling and throwing the board...

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.700
C-Could you please forget that?

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:21.120
Anyways! If he left a legacy,
let's use it for the company!

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.040
Um, but in order to claim it--

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.790
We'll be back soon!

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:26.830
Right...

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.620
<i>Let's dive right into today's letters</i>

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.120
<i>It's "Personal Advice" and the title is</i>

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.120
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:56.700
<i>Hey, hear me out.</i>
<i>There's something I really wanna say</i>

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:01.950
<i>You've got courage to follow</i>
<i>your dreams which is why I chose you</i>

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.080
<i>Is it a risky bet</i>

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.540
<i>Despite no experience,</i>
<i>we jumped right in together</i>

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.000
<i>And this unpredictable story</i>

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:19.080
<i>Is your creation--</i>
<i>a heart-throbbing innovation</i>

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.540
<i>Quickly! Quickly! Take me along</i>

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.160
<i>On a bittersweet love venture</i>

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.950
<i>Ah! Measured not by skill</i>
<i>but by scale and romance</i>

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:34.000
<i>Hurry! Hurry! Boldly, subtly, show your appeal</i>

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.040
<i>Ah! Our meeting was a miracle</i>
<i>that can't be neglected</i>

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.660
<i>It's galactic level</i>

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.160
<i>I see. Sounds like you're head over heels.</i>

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.450
<i>Let's tell him, just like battle</i>

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.830
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.200
<i>Everyone, Hurry! Hurry Love! Love!!</i>

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:00.830
"Episode Two: Inheritance"

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.750
This is the museum.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.790
There's so much stuff!

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:10.330
It's mostly treasure and equipment
from dungeons on display.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:16.580
Like swords that talk, Grim Reaper katanas,
and even holy robes of the zodiac.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.330
It's like a treasure trove in here.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:24.910
I'd love to spend a day giving you a tour
of the place, but now's not the time.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.370
Oh, yeah. That's true.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:30.700
Excuse me. We're from Kibou Company.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.410
Hello. What can I do for you?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.910
I heard the last president gave
his legacy to this museum.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.580
Kibou Company, did you say?
Just one moment please.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.450
Yes, you're absolutely right.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.620
For real?

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.950
Yes. Would you like to see it?

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.330
Of course!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.160
It's right this way.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.000
So this is his legacy...

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.660
It's got everything!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:06.330
Having all this would solve
our equipment problems!

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.870
Um, I'd like to take these back.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.450
Yes, and you may.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.580
In that case, I'd like--

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:15.950
However, you must pay
an inheritance tax in order to claim it.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:16.620
Huh?

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.660
Inheritance tax?

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.000
Because the former owner is currently missing,

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.540
by law, he is presumed to be dead in absentia.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.750
While this permits his legacy to be inherited,

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.000
an inheritance tax must be paid to claim it.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.450
H-How much of a tax are we talking about?

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.700
Roughly this amount.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.450
Th-That much?!

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.370
That's like a hundred yearly salaries...

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.120
You sure it's got that many zeros?

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.870
Yes, I'm sorry to say.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.200
Oh, my. It's really that much?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.200
Yes.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.080
I didn't think about inheritance tax.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.450
I'm sorry. I tried to tell you, but...

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.000
We need his legacy because
we're out of money, yet...

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.000
In order to get it,
we need to pay the tax first.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.330
Talk about a downward spiral.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.870
Yeah. What can we do?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:19.370
B-But, hey! If we pay the tax,
we should be fine, right?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:25.120
"If" we can pay. We'll never amass
that much through normal means.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.750
Once you give up, it's game over.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.370
President...

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.450
Once you give up, it's game over, huh?

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:35.450
A common saying spoken by the wise.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.870
Yeah, but I'm sick of hearing it.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:42.040
A-Anyways, it's not like you to look so down.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:45.450
Let's put our heads together
and figure this out!

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:48.290
Hmm. I don't know what to tell ya.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:51.540
In that case, how about stocks?

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:52.330
Stocks?

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.160
Day trading and investing and such.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:59.330
But don't you need some capital
to make any sort of profit?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:04.370
That's right. It's not very feasible
with our current funds.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:06.160
I see...

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.450
Oh! A slaby race!

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.830
Guessing first place lets you live a comfy life!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:16.410
Gambling, huh?
There's still the risk of guessing wrong.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:20.910
How about the Dream Great lottery?!
First place sets you up for life!

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.200
B-But that's gambling too.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.620
Sheesh! So many complaints!

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:29.370
I still haven't heard any great ideas from you.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.250
Huh, me? Um...

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.290
S-Side gigs?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.790
Denied.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.580
Th-Thought so.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.120
Um, President?

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.790
How about this?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:48.250
Hmm? What?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.160
I saw this posted as a flyer.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:56.580
Let's see... Taking applicants for
the "8th Good Adventure Contest."

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.160
Right. It's run by the Adventure Agency.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.200
There're rewards if you place high enough...

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:07.700
...and first place gets priority
job selection from the Agency.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.540
Huh? That's perfect!

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.870
Yeah! It's everything we need!

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.750
The Agency can supply us with tons of work!

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.330
It gets my approval.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:20.120
Awesome! Great job finding that!

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:24.830
I-I didn't do much.
I just happened to stumble upon it.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.660
No! It's all thanks to your
hard work and dedication!

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.870
Yet another overused line.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.080
He's stealing 'em from somewhere.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:35.620
Perhaps from a management handbook.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.000
President?

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.750
A-Anyways, let's head to the Agency.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.660
President?

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.700
Before that, what about this bill?

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.040
C-Can we expense it?

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.290
You're asking the impossible.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.620
G-Go figure.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:04.370
The "Good Adventure Contest?"
Yes, you may apply.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:06.540
President!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:10.580
Yeah! In that case,
please register "Kibou Company."

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:15.120
Very well. Allow me to explain
the rules of the contest.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.700
The agency has selected a dungeon,
"Order Abbey,"

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:28.250
which you'll explore to obtain
kirakuri with an order form attached.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:33.950
The first company to overcome
the many trials and retrieve it wins.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:35.160
That's it.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.120
Thanks.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:40.250
Please go to the dungeon
on the day of the contest.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.750
Roger that!

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.200
Isn't it great that we got in?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:48.950
Yeah! Let's do our best to get first!
That would be awesome!

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:52.830
--You've got high hopes!
--Isn't that woman with Kibou Company?

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:57.200
I get it! The Kibou guys must be competing too!

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:00.580
Excellent! Now I'm even more pumped up!

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.910
So this is Order Abbey.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:14.290
Yes. If we win this contest,
we can land a reward and more work.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.790
We can pay off the tax and the legacy is ours.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:21.870
Come on, let's rock this!

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.040
I can't wait!

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.370
Yet another reward will be ours!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.790
All these people are in it?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:33.330
I've spotted the best of Imperial
and other top-class companies too.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.160
Top-class...? The best...?

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:43.000
It'll be fine! You might be our captain,
but we're all in the same boat together!

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.160
What if I sink our ship?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:51.540
Anyways, I'm saying not to worry!
We're gonna take first place for sure!

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.330
I wonder about that!

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:59.660
It won't be you taking first place,
but us, Cyedge!

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:05.120
It's been a while, Akari!
I've longed for this day!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.830
Y-You're...!

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.410
Y-You're...!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.410
Who again?

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.290
You're saying you forgot me?!

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.750
You know, it's on tip of my tongue...

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:26.620
Adventure Tech! Adventure Skills Technical School!
We were in the same class!

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.410
Ah...

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.620
S-Such a weak reaction...

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.200
Oh! Was it Saber?!

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.790
It's Rivar!

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.370
Wh-Who's that?

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:39.750
A classmate of my sister's
that thinks they're huge rivals...

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:45.000
...who's one of the members that started
the company Cyedge, I guess?

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:49.290
Lately, Cyedge has become
quite famous as a start-up.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.370
Is that right?

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:55.540
Y-You! How could you forget about me?!

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.450
You're too damn close! Shoo!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:03.330
Okay! Let's just leave it at that!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:08.370
The reason we're here is to win the contest.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:12.080
This is no time to be having a lover's quarrel.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.200
Huh?! Lover's quarrel?!

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.160
Y-You're right, Valmi.

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:20.200
You guys are together?
You're part of this contest too?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:26.040
Of course we are. We'll crush Kibou Company
like the ants that you are!

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:29.450
Excuse me?! Don't you badmouth our company!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.910
It's not badmouthing. It's true.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.450
Grr!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.290
A-Akari!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.330
We appreciate everyone's patience.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:41.080
Hey!

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.290
It's finally time!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:46.160
Thanks for coming, everyone!

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:53.620
I'm proud to announce that the
"8th Good Adventure Contest" is about to begin!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:14:00.580
The goal of our participants
is to explore Order Abbey...

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:05.500
...and retrieve the kirakuri
with an order form from its depths!

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:08.410
Now then, is everyone ready?!

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:13.000
Fantastic!

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.750
Ready! Set! Go!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.250
Hmph! Outta my way!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.410
Come on, President! Let's go!

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:27.200
Huh? W-Wait!

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.410
So this is Order Abbey...

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:40.330
It didn't seem terribly deep to me,
but there sure are a lot of paths.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:45.160
Tsk! They're already gone.
That Gaybar guy is pretty fast.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.790
It's Rivar, Sis.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.750
Akari, what's your relationship with him?

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:56.540
There is no relationship. We were just
classmates and he's kind of a terrible guy.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:00.870
A terrible guy?
He did seem a bit unpleasant, but...

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:06.250
Just talking to him made me remember.
The guy wouldn't leave me alone.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:10.200
One-sidedly trying to compete
with me on grades...

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:15.500
Purposely eating the SS special meal
after seeing I bought the B meal...

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:20.500
Saying "You can come too if you want"
and flaunting all his jobs...

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.160
He's totally the worst!

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:27.450
And after we graduated,
he kept saying "Come to Cyedge!"

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.410
I refused, of course.

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:33.540
I think it's pretty obvious
he just wanted your attention.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:38.700
All right! Enough of the reminiscing,
because we've got company!

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.290
Oh, maju!

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:48.330
Good grief! I'll wipe the floor
with you as stress relief!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:16:00.620
That was too easy! So much for stress relief!

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.660
You clearly took it out on 'em.

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:03.660
Tsk!

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.790
Hmph. What a pathetic bunch.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:14.910
Maju gave you that much trouble?
It would've taken me five seconds!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:18.910
Gah! Not again! What are you, a stalker?!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.120
--I-I'm not! I just wanted to see
how pitiful you guys were...

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:24.620
--Keep moving, President! Jeez, what a creep!
--I-I'm not! I just wanted to see
how pitiful you guys were...

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.450
--...and watch and laugh from afar...
--Um, shouldn't I stamp those?

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.330
You can do that later!

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:30.910
R-Right.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.000
Oh, my. Is this a dead end?

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.870
It looks like something's there.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.250
There's letters.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.700
When is a contract established?

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:55.660
One. When you order a product
and the clerk approves.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.040
Two. When the product arrives.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.540
Three. When you pay for the product.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:05.120
Huh? This is a business question!

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:10.120
You can't proceed unless you press
one of these three and solve the question.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:15.370
Well? You guys think you know the answer?

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:21.200
Don't tell me you're just bugging us
because you don't know it yourself!

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.200
Y-Yeah, right! How rude!

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:27.040
In that case, answer if you dare!

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.580
V-Very well!

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:33.040
This one is simple. The answer is...

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.040
The answer, you see...

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.120
...is this!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:42.290
As usual, all bark and no bite.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.580
Sh-Shut up! I'd like to see you do better!

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:52.290
The answer is one. "When you order
a product and the clerk approves."

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.120
What?!

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:04.620
A contract can be established by two parties
making a verbal agreement.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:06.410
How's that?!

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:07.790
See ya later!

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.870
Tsk! That man...!

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:17.950
I see... I was right to keep
a watchful eye on him.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.330
Um...

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:26.450
What is the repayment amount after three years?

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:28.750
An interest calculation, huh?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:31.120
The amount after three years?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:36.080
Um, one year would be 150,000 gold, so...

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.410
You called?!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:42.450
That question is so simple! The answer...

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.040
The answer is...!

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.200
1,520,875 gold.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.080
So fast!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.950
I knew I was right about you!

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.080
What a braniac!

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:59.790
Gee, I don't know...

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:02.750
Wait right there! Who are you?!

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:05.040
Huh? You mean me?

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:11.580
I've seen you strutting around!
What's your relationship with Akari?!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:16.910
Our relationship?
Basically, I'm president and she's an employee.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:20.080
What? You're the new president?!

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.250
With that scrawny little body?

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.950
I-I'm sorry.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.950
Hey! Don't make fun of our president!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:31.370
Sure, he's not suited for battle,
but he's trying his best!

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:34.450
Y-You didn't have to follow with that.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.950
What's your adventurer rank?

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.200
Huh? I'm two stars, but...

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:45.620
It takes just a month to get two stars
after becoming an adventurer!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:49.410
You being president says
a lot about Kibou Company!

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.290
Sheesh, just shut up!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:55.790
By the way, I'm four stars!
And Valmi here is five!

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.830
Rank isn't everything!

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:02.580
Our president is way more capable than you are!

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:03.540
Maybe...

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:06.080
More than me?

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.200
Then, how about a bet?

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.120
A bet?

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:14.700
If we win this contest, Akari,
you've gotta join Cyedge!

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.000
Wha--?!

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:17.410
Job poacher!

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.580
That's some pretty bold headhunting there!

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:24.000
Kibou Company lets your abilities go to waste.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:28.250
I'll give our HR the heads-up.
Well? How about it?

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:30.870
Why would I join your company?

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.620
What's the matter? Afraid to lose?

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.120
Grr!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:39.160
--C-Calm down, Akari.
--And how about if I win?!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.830
I'll grovel, dance naked, or whatever you want!

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:46.700
I don't wanna see it, but you're on!
Don't forget your promise!

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.700
Fine! It's settled then.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:54.040
I'm looking forward to when
you come and join us!

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.910
A-Are you sure about making a promise like that?

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.580
What?! We've just gotta win!

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:06.700
B-But...

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:12.450
Doesn't it make you mad?!
He's totally making fun of our company!

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:13.870
Akari...

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:18.040
Well, it makes me mad!
It's just like insulting my family!

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:23.700
You're right. Yeah... Let's win!

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:27.120
I never wanna work in
a different place than you.

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:30.120
We'll definitely stop him from poaching you.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:33.410
Akari's an invaluable part of Kibou company!

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:36.040
Yup!

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:44.040
Rivar? Was it okay to make a promise like that?

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.160
Of course it's okay.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:50.950
Don't worry, Akari's talented.
She'll handle the switch just fine.

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.750
That's not what I mean. What about if you lose?

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:56.120
If I lose?

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:02.330
Their president has a rank of two stars.
There's no way we lose.

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:04.370
Let's hope that's true.

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:09.660
More importantly, let's hurry up.
I'm more worried about other companies.

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:11.700
All righty!

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:13.910
--We might be able to pull this off!
--Still, that president of theirs...

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:17.500
--Yeah! Let's keep up the good pace!
--Still, that president of theirs...

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.500
I'm pretty sure he's...

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:43.290
<i>Looking way up into the night sky</i>

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:47.910
<i>A pretty jewel caught my eye</i>

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:52.250
<i>Clear skies tomorrow sure would be nice</i>

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:56.370
<i>Now, make a wish upon a star</i>

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:58.450
<i>Lazily</i>

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:01.290
<i>Today comes to a close</i>

00:23:01.290 --> 00:23:05.660
<i>Dead tired and worn out</i>

00:23:05.660 --> 00:23:12.160
<i>Good work</i>
<i>Let's do our best again tomorrow</i>

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:14.750
<i>Goodnight</i>

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:16.910
<i>Every day is sparkling</i>

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:21.450
<i>Just like a box of jewels (sparkling)</i>

00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:23.660
<i>And so brilliant</i>

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:25.870
<i>Any work undone</i>

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:30.450
<i>We'll leave for dreamland (sleep tight)</i>

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:33.950
<i>Let's embark on adventure</i>

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:38.250
<i>So sleep soundly tonight</i>

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:43.500
<i>And meet up with me in our dreams</i>

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:46.580
<i>Sleep tight</i>
